  "index": 3,
  "response": "**Summary:**\n\nThe North Atlantic Treaty outlines the commitment of its signatories to:\n\n**1. Peaceful Resolution of Disputes:**\n- Resolving international disputes peacefully, prioritizing peace and security.\n- Refraining from the threat or use of force.\n\n**2. Promoting Friendly International Relations:**\n- Strengthening free institutions and understanding their principles.\n- Promoting stability and well-being.\n- Eliminating conflicts in economic policies and encouraging collaboration.\n\n**3. Self-Defense Capabilities:**\n- Maintaining and developing individual and collective capacity to resist armed attacks.\n\n**4. Collective Defense:**\n- Treating an armed attack on any signatory in Europe or North America as an attack on all.\n- Providing mutual assistance in defending the North Atlantic area.",
